// foundry-tools' local Renovate config, on top of renovate-config's global
// config.js (which says "drop a renovate.json into a repo to override
// locally"). It is a repo file because Renovate autodiscovers this fleet, and
// autodiscovery discards per-repo objects in a global `repositories` list. A
// global packageRule cannot reach this setting either: a vulnerability rule
// takes its `force` from the package file's vulnerabilityAlerts, not from any
// rule.
{
  // VULNERABILITY BUMPS ARE OFF HERE UNTIL 2026-12-01 (Rob, 2026-10-05).
  // OSV's fixes for GO-2026-6508 (otlploggrpc) and GO-2026-6615 (otel/sdk/log)
  // are v0.21.0. That pulls otel/log v0.21.0, whose API
  // github.com/dagger/otel-go@v1.43.0 (the latest release) does not compile
  // against: 13 undefined symbols, the module cannot load, and every
  // foundry-tools rollup since 2026-09-28 has been red on it. A vulnerability
  // rule's allowedVersions overrides the hold in config.js
  // ("OpenTelemetry Go log family held below the v0.21 API break").
  //
  // With this off, a vulnerable dependency gets no bump at all here. The gate
  // still grades the vulnerabilities: govulncheck runs on every pull and
  // accepts only the two allowances in internal/checks/vulnallow.go, which
  // expire 2026-12-01.
  //
  // RE-ENABLE (delete this file) when a dagger/otel-go release builds against
  // otel/log v0.21.0+, or on 2026-12-01 when those allowances lapse, whichever
  // comes first.
  vulnerabilityAlerts: { enabled: false },
}
